  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: S. Giovanni di Sinis</p>\r\n<div>\u00a0</div>\r\n<div>Smith 1857 (2.1135) emphasizes that the site is mentioned by Ptolemy as <em>Tarrae</em> or <em>Tarras</em> and also in the Antonine Itineraries, which place it 12 miles from Othoca.</div>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An ancient Phoenician settlement located in western Sardinia on a promontory in the Gulf of Oristano, just south of modern San Giovanni di Sinis. While it originates as a Punic or Carthaginian settlement ca. 700 BCE, it continued as a major town in Roman times.",
